WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.000
[Part 1: The Longest Hour — Tense Pulsing Synth-Bass & Terminal Atmosphere]

00:00:25.000 --> 00:01:25.000
[Driving Industrial Synthwave Beat — Anxious Wait at Sea-Tac]

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:50.000
[Atmospheric Synth Breakdown — Scanning the Terminal Crowd]

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:50.000
[Urgent Industrial Arpeggios & Percussion Build]

00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:20.000
[Quiet Melodic Interlude — A Familiar Voice Breaks Through]

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:59.500
[Part 2: My Anchor (Reunion) — Driving Synthwave & Rock Guitar Intro]

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.000
Searching faces in the crowd

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.500
A silent scream that's screaming loud

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:10.000
Just one more hall, just one more sign

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.500
This can't be real, this friend of mine

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.500
They said you're here, alone and lost

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.000
I'll find you, friend, no matter the cost

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.500
A thousand miles of fear and pain

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.500
Left standing in the pouring rain

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.000
But I see you there, so small and lost

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.500
My broken friend, whatever the cost

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.500
I'm running to you, hold on tight

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.500
I am your anchor in this night

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.500
The storm has passed, the waiting's through

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.500
My dearest friend, I'm here for you

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:49.000
I've got you now, you're safe with me

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:56.000
For all the world to finally see

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:23.000
[Soaring 80s Electric Guitar Solo Battles the Industrial Static]

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:49.000
[Driving Industrial Synthwave & Arpeggio Interlude]

00:05:49.000 --> 00:06:11.000
[Melodic Lead Guitar Triumphs Over the Synth-Bass]

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.500
That hooded sweatshirt, soaked and thin

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.500
The cold November's gotten in

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:21.500
You're shivering now, your face is pale

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.000
Behind a thin and broken veil

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.500
Of pride and fear, I see it all

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:32.000
The quiet terror of the fall

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.000
She left you here without a coat

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.500
A wordless scream caught in your throat

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.000
[Dramatic Drum Fill]

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.000
And I'm running to you, hold on tight

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.000
I am your anchor in this night

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
The storm has passed, the waiting's through

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.000
My dearest friend, I'm here for you

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.000
I've got you now, you're safe with me

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:10.000
For all the world to finally see

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:31.000
[Triumphant 80s Arena Rock Guitar Solo — The Mask Falls]

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:50.320
[Cathartic Synthwave & Rock Finale]
